        "original_id": "302f9398-ddc2-5bfa-9dae-de43a8faea36",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Liaoyang, Changchun, Liaoning province, Jilin province, T'ai-tzu River, China\n- People: Yuan Baojing\n- Organizations: Northeast Normal University\n- Concepts: prefecture-level cities, metro areas, national normal universities, population census\n\nFacts:\n- Yuan Baojing was born on 16 February 1966 and was a Chinese billionaire from Liaoyang in Liaoning province.\n- In 2010, Liaoyang in east-central Liaoning province was situated on the T'ai-tzu River and, together with Anshan, formed a metro area with 2,057,200 inhabitants.\n- According to the 2010 census of China, Changchun had a total population of 7,674,439 under its jurisdiction.\n- Northeast Normal University is located in Changchun in Jilin province and is one of the six national normal universities in the People's Republic of China.\n- Yuan Baojing died on 17 March 2006.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
